<title>UK: Hanson rebounds on bottom-trading.</title>
<headline>Hanson rebounds on bottom-trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hanson Plc rebounded sharply on heavy trading volume on Wednesday amid perceptions the stock was oversold, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1505 GMT, the shares were up 10-1/2p, or 3.8 percent, to 287 on trading volume of 10.5 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;The shares were very oversold and they were looking cheap. People have been trying to call a bottom for a long time,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Another noted that Merrill Lynch recently issued a buy recommendation on the stock, targeting the 348p level. --London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
